---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="browser-agent">

          <p>
            The browser is a real Chromium view embedded in the Vector window, not a screenshot service, and it is
            attached to the current repository and session. Open a local preview or URL, interact manually, or ask
            Vector to inspect and test the page as part of the engineering task.
          </p>

          <h2 id="controlled-browser">Observe, repair, retest</h2>
          <p>
            The agent opens the running product, clicks and types, reads console and network failures, captures what
            it saw, repairs the code, and retests.
          </p>

          <h2 id="sensitive-steps">Sign-in and sensitive steps</h2>
          <p>
            The agent refuses to type into password, one-time-code and card fields. It pauses and hands the live
            browser to you, then resumes with what it can see.
          </p>
          <div class="do-dont">
            <article>
              <strong>Good uses</strong>
              <p>Local UI testing, console inspection, screenshots, documentation research, and approved deployment workflows.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <strong>Approval stays visible</strong>
              <p>Take over for sign-in, secrets, payments, destructive changes, and other sensitive actions.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
</DocsPage>
